HST Office: Worksheet.ListObjects: Excel tables in VBA; CommandBars no longer fails.

7% of the macro files use tables. ListObjects, ListObject (Name, Range, DataBodyRange, HeaderRowRange,
TotalsRowRange, ShowTotals, Resize, Unlist, Delete), ListColumns and ListRows (Count, by index or name,
For Each, Add, Delete, Range, DataBodyRange) on the database ranges that Excel tables are imported to.
ListObjects.Add makes one. TableStyle is kept, not drawn.

Application.CommandBars failed in every document: the VBA context holds no singletons, so it is asked of
the process context.

The new files are for HST Office under MPL-2.0, like the files around them.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/vba-corpus/regression_cases.py (ListObjects*, CommandBars*).
